  "problem_context": {
    "problem_statement": "Keep the existing exact prefix-node-suffix strong contract as strong_spec and add three common named specifications directly derived from it: remove_member_spec, remove_front_spec, and remove_tail_spec. The member specification removes only the first occurrence via a custom Coq function xizi_sll_remove_first. The C implementation and ABI must remain unchanged, and all generated derivation witnesses must be proved.",
    "target_function": "xizi_single_link_remove_node",
    "expected_behavior": "For the real netdev_unregister call, remove_member_spec is the default client view: membership is known, return value is ignored, and ownership of the detached node_next field is required for later overwrite. Front and tail specifications are convenience specializations.",
    "input_output_contract": "strong_spec preserves the current exact result, remaining list app(l1,l2), and detached node old successor. remove_member_spec requires In(node,l) and ensures head(remove_first node l) * xizi_sll_node(node). remove_front_spec requires head(node::suffix) and ensures head(suffix) * xizi_sll_node(node). remove_tail_spec requires head(prefix++[node]) and ensures head(prefix) * xizi_sll_node(node). Simplified specs intentionally omit return equality and the old node_next value.",
    "spec_hint": [
      "Define xizi_sll_remove_first in the case_lib with Z.eq_dec and return the tail immediately on the first match; do not use Coq.Lists.List.remove because it removes all equal occurrences. Add named forward declarations using remove_member_spec <= strong_spec, remove_front_spec <= strong_spec, and remove_tail_spec <= strong_spec, then verify the implementation under strong_spec."
    ],
    "preferred_hidden_properties": [
      "Membership yields a first-hit decomposition l = prefix ++ node :: suffix with node absent from prefix, so xizi_sll_remove_first node l = prefix ++ suffix.",
      "The exact detached node_next points-to assertion plus non-nullness entails xizi_sll_node for the simplified postconditions."
    ],
    "forbidden_patterns": [
      "Do not use QCP_demos_human or Applications_human as references.",
      "Do not replace first-removal semantics with Coq List.remove or any remove-all operator.",
      "Do not weaken or alter the existing strong_spec, mirror the C traversal as a new Rocq algorithm, hand-edit generated files, add Admitted/Axiom, or use forbidden lemmas."
    ],
